1
00:00:00,769 --> 00:00:04,249
So we had a look at out-of-band swaps, which

2
00:00:04,506 --> 00:00:05,869
can be a useful feature.

3
00:00:06,446 --> 00:00:09,830
Now, there is another swap-related feature,

4
00:00:10,311 --> 00:00:13,214
not out-of-band swap, but swap in general,

5
00:00:13,984 --> 00:00:16,245
that also might come in handy in certain

6
00:00:16,245 --> 00:00:16,919
situations.

7
00:00:17,833 --> 00:00:20,944
Let's say here in my list of places, I'm

8
00:00:20,944 --> 00:00:23,927
selecting one of the last places here, maybe

9
00:00:24,103 --> 00:00:25,178
the last place.

10
00:00:26,188 --> 00:00:29,061
If I do that, it gets added to this list up

11
00:00:29,061 --> 00:00:31,726
here, of course. Now maybe we wanna make

12
00:00:31,774 --> 00:00:34,888
sure that the browser automatically

13
00:00:35,819 --> 00:00:38,900
scrolls up to that upper list therefore and

14
00:00:39,013 --> 00:00:42,271
focuses this list when we add an item.

15
00:00:43,266 --> 00:00:45,289
And that's something which we can also

16
00:00:45,353 --> 00:00:47,680
implement with help of HTMX.

17
00:00:48,948 --> 00:00:50,778
All we have to do for that is

18
00:00:51,372 --> 00:00:55,096
go to the place where we define the swapping

19
00:00:55,304 --> 00:00:58,289
mechanism or the swapping script. Strategy,

20
00:00:58,770 --> 00:01:00,917
if you wanna call it like this, for the

21
00:01:00,981 --> 00:01:01,799
loaded content.

22
00:01:02,761 --> 00:01:05,646
And then we can add some extra settings to

23
00:01:06,030 --> 00:01:07,088
hx-swap.

24
00:01:07,970 --> 00:01:11,785
Thus far, we focused on these settings here,

25
00:01:12,073 --> 00:01:15,070
so on the swapping strategy when using

26
00:01:15,327 --> 00:01:16,385
hx-swap.

27
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:19,061
And that of course makes a lot of sense

28
00:01:19,174 --> 00:01:21,770
because it is indeed the strategy

29
00:01:22,395 --> 00:01:25,729
that you'll probably adjust in most cases.

30
00:01:26,403 --> 00:01:28,633
Sometimes you might wanna swap just the

31
00:01:28,633 --> 00:01:30,735
content inside of the target element.

32
00:01:31,297 --> 00:01:33,239
Sometimes you might wanna replace the entire

33
00:01:33,367 --> 00:01:36,496
target element or add an element to the end

34
00:01:36,496 --> 00:01:37,491
of the target element.

35
00:01:38,036 --> 00:01:40,893
So it makes sense to know these values.

36
00:01:41,711 --> 00:01:43,813
And the official documentation is a great

37
00:01:43,813 --> 00:01:46,910
place to look up these values in case you

38
00:01:46,926 --> 00:01:47,696
forgot about one.

39
00:01:49,028 --> 00:01:51,884
But there are actually more things you can

40
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:53,569
configure with hx-select.

41
00:01:54,627 --> 00:01:58,010
You can, for example, add some delays so

42
00:01:58,250 --> 00:01:59,212
that HTMX

43
00:01:59,757 --> 00:02:02,947
waits until the received response content is

44
00:02:03,155 --> 00:02:04,582
swapped into the DOM.

45
00:02:05,448 --> 00:02:08,269
And that can be useful for playing some

46
00:02:08,349 --> 00:02:11,475
animation, but you can, for example, also

47
00:02:11,475 --> 00:02:15,146
control the scrolling behavior of the target

48
00:02:15,146 --> 00:02:15,466
element.

49
00:02:16,588 --> 00:02:19,185
If you're swapping content into a list

50
00:02:19,233 --> 00:02:21,750
that's scrollable, you could, for example,

51
00:02:21,959 --> 00:02:25,501
add the scroll setting to tell HTMX to

52
00:02:25,501 --> 00:02:29,193
scroll to the top or bottom of that list,

53
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:32,114
or if you wanna scroll to the entire

54
00:02:32,306 --> 00:02:34,344
element. So if you wanna scroll the entire

55
00:02:34,553 --> 00:02:37,346
element into view and make it visible, you

56
00:02:37,378 --> 00:02:39,528
could use the show modifier.

57
00:02:40,507 --> 00:02:43,284
And you add those modifiers by simply adding

58
00:02:43,316 --> 00:02:45,258
them after your strategy

59
00:02:45,964 --> 00:02:47,296
separated by a whitespace.

60
00:02:47,826 --> 00:02:50,025
So you have your strategy and then you add

61
00:02:50,057 --> 00:02:50,827
your modifiers

62
00:02:51,485 --> 00:02:53,572
and you can therefore then add this extra

63
00:02:53,572 --> 00:02:56,477
configuration to your element.

64
00:02:57,776 --> 00:03:00,119
So in our case here, if I wanna make sure

65
00:03:00,633 --> 00:03:05,046
that I show this target element whenever it

66
00:03:05,046 --> 00:03:08,368
is edited, so whenever I added a new place

67
00:03:08,416 --> 00:03:09,924
to my interesting locations,

68
00:03:10,823 --> 00:03:13,647
I can achieve this by adding the show

69
00:03:14,032 --> 00:03:14,819
modifier here

70
00:03:15,428 --> 00:03:18,269
separated by a whitespace from the strategy.

71
00:03:19,665 --> 00:03:22,200
And then I can add a colon after show to

72
00:03:22,216 --> 00:03:22,585
control

73
00:03:23,356 --> 00:03:25,137
what exactly I wanna show here.

74
00:03:26,152 --> 00:03:29,168
So if I wanna move the browser to the top of

75
00:03:29,378 --> 00:03:31,667
the target element or to the bottom, and

76
00:03:31,684 --> 00:03:33,006
here I wanna move it to the top.

77
00:03:35,146 --> 00:03:38,584
And now by adding this here to hx-swap, when

78
00:03:38,696 --> 00:03:41,990
we send that POST request, I'll achieve the

79
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:43,195
desired behavior.

80
00:03:44,143 --> 00:03:46,920
Now if I reload the page and I click on one

81
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:48,149
of the last elements here,

82
00:03:48,747 --> 00:03:52,304
you see the browser scrolls that entire list

83
00:03:52,304 --> 00:03:54,908
here into view, that list into which the

84
00:03:54,908 --> 00:03:55,226
element is rendered.

85
00:03:57,310 --> 00:03:59,479
Now maybe I don't just wanna scroll that

86
00:03:59,479 --> 00:04:00,331
list into view,

87
00:04:00,861 --> 00:04:04,091
but instead that section in which that list

88
00:04:04,091 --> 00:04:04,605
is rendered.

89
00:04:05,585 --> 00:04:07,867
And that's also something we can achieve

90
00:04:07,931 --> 00:04:10,903
with show because as you also see in the

91
00:04:10,903 --> 00:04:12,125
official documentation,

92
00:04:12,751 --> 00:04:16,318
you can specify a CSS selector with scroll

93
00:04:16,607 --> 00:04:20,046
or show so that you actually show another

94
00:04:20,126 --> 00:04:23,387
element than the target element, with this

95
00:04:23,677 --> 00:04:24,383
modifier.

96
00:04:25,218 --> 00:04:29,170
So here in my case, it is that section here

97
00:04:29,298 --> 00:04:31,402
that I wanna scroll into view,

98
00:04:32,109 --> 00:04:34,550
that section that has this interesting

99
00:04:34,582 --> 00:04:36,060
locations list inside of it.

100
00:04:37,008 --> 00:04:39,417
And therefore I'll simply assign an ID to

101
00:04:39,417 --> 00:04:42,115
that section to have a quick and easy way of

102
00:04:42,163 --> 00:04:42,726
selecting it.

103
00:04:43,432 --> 00:04:44,155
And I'll name it

104
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:46,853
int locations section,

105
00:04:47,528 --> 00:04:48,315
something like that.

106
00:04:49,925 --> 00:04:51,810
And if I now use that ID here

107
00:04:52,784 --> 00:04:54,262
with my show modifier

108
00:04:54,879 --> 00:04:57,525
after a colon by selecting it like this,

109
00:04:59,346 --> 00:05:01,958
then I'll make sure that I actually scroll

110
00:05:02,022 --> 00:05:04,391
the browser to the top of this section

111
00:05:04,972 --> 00:05:07,106
after this POST request here succeeded.

112
00:05:08,816 --> 00:05:10,413
So with those changes made,

113
00:05:11,349 --> 00:05:13,657
if we reload this page and again add one of

114
00:05:13,657 --> 00:05:16,278
the last elements, You see, we scroll up to

115
00:05:16,310 --> 00:05:18,290
the top of this section.

116
00:05:19,674 --> 00:05:21,927
And that's therefore another useful feature

117
00:05:21,943 --> 00:05:23,891
and behavior you should be aware of.
